Z||000016||stimpy||10-23-2000||06:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steven:<BR><B>What dealer charged you $7.00 for that V6-H.O. name plate. I just priced it and the dealers are selling them for 3.35 plus tax. Heck they only pay $2.01. And this is for ANY color. You were boned. DOOOOPPPPPP!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Remind me to cry into my pillow tonight. I feel so used.<P>I learned a long time ago that someone will always say they got it bigger, better, faster, cheaper.  If you can buy them all day at $3.35 from your friendly GM dealer, then get on with yer bad self, buy up a bunch and sell em. I know at least one sucker who was willing to pay $7. Of course, at that time I was being an innovator, not an imitator. And people think it looks cool. <P>So there. :P||||reg||1
Z||000017||Seanh||10-23-2000||07:39 PM||||Well, I called around to see who in town does powder coating, and found, no ones does. Great. The closest place is in hastings, ne, about 2.5 hours away. I called them and told them what I would like to have done. They said for doing the upper and mid intake manifold, throttle body, and the heatshields would cost about $200-250 with shipping. I cant see paying that, probally would be worth it though. I think, since hearing that people have been having good results with using regular engine enamal, that I will try it. The parts I am going to do wouldnt really be too hard to take off again if it flakes. So, I am going to do that, and, if I have problems, I will go for powder coating. Also, one other question: I am going to replace the vacuum hoses with Rodneys kit, what color do you think I should paint them given my other choices for engine colors above? I was thinking white, but I would think it might look better some other color. What do ya think?<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
